      "side": 1,
      "message": "A per-request stream channel doesn\u0027t just fire one of these three callbacks and stop; successful request still ends with the stream closing afterward. So the real sequence for an ordinary successful request is:\n\n1 - channelRead0(response) - callback.onSuccess(response).\n2 - The stream then closes - channelInactive() fires too.\n\nWithout the completed guard, step 2 would also call callback.onFailure(new ClosedChannelException()) — turning every single successful request into a second, failure completion right after the real success.\nSame approach is used in TestRequestCallback:",
